      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nDFLASH-family draft KV memory sizing currently shards the draft model's KV heads by the global tensor-parallel size. With DP attention, the attention tensor-parallel width can be smaller than the global TP width, so this underestimates the draft KV pool and can over-allocate the shared token capacity until startup runs out of memory.\r\n\r\nFor example, with TP 32, attention TP 1, and 16 draft KV heads, the estimator accounts for one KV head while the draft pool stores all 16 heads on each attention rank: a 16x underestimate of the draft KV term. This is a memory-sizing issue, not an inference-output accuracy bug.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nUse `attn_tp_size` instead of the global `tp_size` when resolving the DFLASH-family draft KV bytes per token. This matches the parallel width used by the actual attention KV pool.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nN/A. This PR only corrects memory sizing. It does not modify model outputs or attention-kernel computation.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nN/A. No throughput or latency claim is made for this change.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). Regression tests are pending.\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). No user-facing API or configuration changes are expected; documentation applicability will be confirmed before marking ready.\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). Not applicable to the current memory-sizing-only revision; no benchmark claim is made.\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n* Common commands include /tag-and-rerun-ci, /tag-run-ci-label, /rerun-failed-ci\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #34451240697](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34451240697)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #34451240557](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34451240557)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:start -->:x: [Run #34451240507](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34451240507)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
